{"agent_id":"pp3g-4xe1-primary-adversarial-review-on-433-a-muse-spark-894c","agent_seq":2,"timestamp":"2026-08-23T22:20:54.530455905Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"ad7c02f7-18fe-4542-9f11-f5c25fc82bb4","comment_uuid":"bbf09248-6759-4b3e-9d6f-e5b913ad51d4","author":"pp3g-4xe1-primary-adversarial-review-on-433-a-muse-spark-894c","content":"PRIMARY ADVERSARIAL REVIEW #433 (hy3, independent of muse-spark pass) — FINDINGS PART 1/3 (A,B,C). Lens: re-derive from source, distrust doc self-claims.\n\nFINDING A [MUST-FIX / launch-blocking] Replan doc structurally incompatible with crosslink fork design_doc parser.\n- statement: .design/epic-423-swarm-replan.md is marked 'consumed_by: crosslink swarm init --doc' but uses ONLY H1 ('#') headings ('# Purpose', '# Phase DIS', '# Phase R0' ... '# Swarm Parameters') and has NO '## Requirements' H2. Source crosslink/src/commands/design_doc.rs: sections switch ONLY on H2 ('## ', line 94); every H1 resets title + section=Title (lines 80-91); flush_block(Title) is a no-op (line 125). So ALL body content between H1s is discarded -> requirements and requirement_groups are EMPTY. swarm/init.rs:18 calls parse_design_doc. Net: 'crosslink swarm init --doc epic-423-swarm-replan.md' parses to a DesignDoc with ZERO work units -> swarm launches nothing.\n- why-unverified: the #423 kickoff (22:03) only edited the PLAN doc and explicitly admitted it 'did NOT verify swarm-init parser behavior.' The replan (the actual consumed_by target) was never checked against the grammar.\n- cheapest discriminating test: run 'crosslink swarm init --doc .design/epic-423-swarm-replan.md' in a scratch worktree and inspect parsed requirement count; or unit-test parse_design_doc(replan_text) -> assert requirement_groups.len() > 0.\n- severity-if-wrong: total swarm init failure (zero agents). MUST FIX before launch.\n\nFINDING B [HIGH] DIS acceptance instance #2 is self-healed; worktree docs still assert it as broken.\n- statement: worktree docs list 'unverifiable playbook section citations reported by issue #429 researcher' as a known-broken DIS instance. But #429 auditor (pp3g-JUF0) posted a PROVENANCE CORRECTION: those citations were phantom-at-write (2026-08-18, playbook absent) and SELF-HEALED (playbook now exists with 5.1-5.9 incl. cited numbers). MAIN repo plan doc (line 9) already corrected this ('four verified current instances' + temporal-healing clause). Worktree copies are stale.\n- why-unverified: worktree docs predate the #429 correction.\n- cheapest discriminating test: confirm agent-orchestration-playbook.md 5.3/5.4/5.6/5.8 exist (they do) -> instance #2 is not currently broken.\n- severity-if-wrong: DIS acceptance gate trains/tests on a phantom -> gate validity undermined. Medium.\n\nFINDING C [HIGH] DIS acceptance instance #4 ('stale git claim in auditor kickoff text') is not locatable; catchability unverifiable.\n- statement: design docs assert a 'stale git claim in auditor kickoff text' as a known-broken instance. I read auditor.md in full, read kickoff-custom-template.md, and grepped /home/claude-code/.crosslink and /home/claude-code/.claude for 'stale git'/'git claim' -> the phrase appears ONLY in the design docs themselves, never at the asserted source. The main repo plan doc still lists it as 'verified current' but I cannot verify that verification.\n- why-unverified: instance source not accessible/identifiable from reviewer scope; may live in built-in KICKOFF.md inside the crosslink binary (not inspectable) or operator private notes.\n- cheapest discriminating test: locate the exact 'stale git claim' string in auditor kickoff text (grep -r 'stale git' ~/.crosslink/rules/kickoff.md and built-in template) and confirm it is both stale and present. Until located, DIS cannot be validated against this instance.\n- severity-if-wrong: if the claim is a phantom (like #2), the DIS 'must catch all four' criterion is unsatisfiable for that instance. Medium-High.","created_at":"2026-08-23T22:20:54.5241